<resources>
  <!--
    Physical pixel pitch in micrometres.

    UdfpsOverlayInteractor.calculateIconSize() derives the fingerprint icon
    size as udfps_icon_size / pixel_pitch. The AOSP default is -1 (unset; only
    Pixel devices ship an override), so iconSize becomes 6000 / -1 = -6000 and
    iconPadding becomes (sensorWidth - iconSize) / 2 = (300 + 6000) / 2 = 3150px.
    That padding is then applied to the 300x300 (radius 150) device entry
    ImageView, squeezing the drawable into a clipped sliver at the top edge
    instead of a centred fingerprint ring.

    25400 / 560dpi = 45.36um, which gives a 6000/45.36 = 132px icon inside the
    300px sensor box (84px padding per side).

    Note: this must live in sm8150-common/overlay (PRODUCT_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS),
    not beyond1q/overlay (DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS). Only the former's RRO is
    installed to /product/overlay, which is the copy SystemUI actually applies.
  -->
  <item name="pixel_pitch" format="float" type="dimen">45.36</item>
</resources>